  "id": "COMPOUND:22069 - PROTEIN:5776",
  "verbalization": "Cocosamide B is implicated in the biological pathway leading to MIP through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Cocosamide B acts as a target for multiple entities, including MOVP-3, SNB-78, and Hepatocyte, all of which are targets of the same compound, 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One. This compound is consistently identified as a target of Cocosamide B across all three paths, with a high confidence score in each case. The shared target relationship between Cocosamide B and 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, and the subsequent targeting of MIP by this latter compound, indicates a potential mechanism where Cocosamide B influences the activity of 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, which in turn affects MIP. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Cocosamide B in modulating the activity of a downstream target, ultimately influencing MIP. The consistent presence of 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One as a common mediator across all three paths strengthens the hypothesis that Cocosamide B interacts with this compound, which then targets MIP.",
